The function is thread-safe by using a mutex to lock access to the logging functionality. It also supports different logging levels (e.g., info, warning, error) and allows configuration of which levels are enabled at runtime. The function can be integrated with an external logging service via a custom API that sends log messages asynchronously to a remote server.

The code includes a feature to automatically rotate log files after reaching a certain size, keeping the disk space usage under control. It also provides an option to suppress logging for specific functions or modules within the application, allowing fine-grained control over which parts of the code are logged. Finally, the function includes a mechanism to detect and handle logging failures gracefully, such as retrying the operation or using an alternative logging method if the primary method fails.']

