The function uses a loop to search for matches of each book name in the text using the regular expression created from the book name. If a match is found, the function increments the count for that book by 1. The function returns an object with the names of the books found as keys and their counts as values.

This function is designed to handle large text inputs efficiently, ensuring that it does not consume excessive memory or processing time. It also supports multiple concurrent requests and does not block other operations in the system. Additionally, this function is extensible, allowing for easy addition of new books or languages in the future."]

