using System;

public class RandomValueGenerator
{
    private int _minValue;
    private int _maxValue;
    private float _minFloatValue;
    private float _maxFloatValue;
    private bool _isInclusiveIntRange;
    private bool _isExclusiveIntRange;
    private bool _isInclusiveFloatRange;
    private bool _isExclusiveFloatRange;
    private int _currentIntValue;
    private float _currentFloatValue;
    private int _sampleCount;

    public RandomValueGenerator(int minValue, int maxValue)
    {
        if (minValue > maxValue)
            throw new ArgumentException("Minimum value must be less than or equal to maximum value.");

        _minValue = minValue;
        _maxValue = maxValue;
        _isInclusiveIntRange = true;
        _isExclusiveIntRange = false;
        Reset();
    }

    public RandomValueGenerator(int minValue, int maxValue, bool isInclusive)
    {
        if (minValue > maxValue)
            throw new ArgumentException("Minimum value must be less than or equal to maximum value.");

        _minValue = minValue;
        _maxValue = maxValue;
        _isInclusiveIntRange = isInclusive;
        _isExclusiveIntRange = !isInclusive;
        Reset();
    }

    public RandomValueGenerator(float minFloatValue, float maxFloatValue)
    {
        if (minFloatValue > maxFloatValue)
            throw new ArgumentException("Minimum value must be less than or equal to maximum value.");

        _minFloatValue = minFloatValue;
        _maxFloatValue = maxFloatValue;
        _isInclusiveFloatRange = true;
        _isExclusiveFloatRange = false;
        Reset();
    }

    public RandomValueGenerator(float minFloatValue, float maxFloatValue, bool isInclusive)
    {
        if (minFloatValue > maxFloatValue)
            throw new ArgumentException("Minimum value must be less than or equal to maximum value.");

        _minFloatValue = minFloatValue;
        _maxFloatValue = maxFloatValue;
        _isInclusiveFloatRange = isInclusive;
        _isExclusiveFloatRange = !isInclusive;
        Reset();
    }

    public int GenerateRandomInt()
    {
        if (_minValue == _maxValue)
            return _minValue;

        var random = new Random();
        var value = random.Next(_minValue, _maxValue + 1);

        if (_isInclusiveIntRange)
            return value;
        else
            return value - 1;
    }

    public float GenerateRandomFloat()
    {
        if (_minFloatValue == _maxFloatValue)
            return _minFloatValue;

        var random = new Random();
        var value = (float)(random.NextDouble() * (_maxFloatValue - _minFloatValue)) + _minFloatValue;

        if (_isInclusiveFloatRange)
            return value;
        else
            return value - 1;
    }

    public void Reset()
    {
        _currentIntValue = _minValue;
        _currentFloatValue = (float)_minFloatValue;
        _sampleCount = 0;
    }

    public int[] GenerateRandomInts(int count)
    {
        if (count <= 0)
            throw new ArgumentException("Invalid number of samples.");

        var values = new int[count];
        for (var i = 0; i < count; i++)
        {
            values[i] = GenerateRandomInt();
        }

        return values;
    }

    public float[] GenerateRandomFloats(int count)
    {
        if (count <= 0)
            throw new ArgumentException("Invalid number of samples.");

        var values = new float[count];
        for (var i = 0; i < count; i++)
        {
            values[i] = GenerateRandomFloat();
        }

        return values;
    }

    public override string ToString()
    {
        if (_minValue == _maxValue)
            return $"{_minValue}";
        else if (_isInclusiveIntRange)
            return $"[{_minValue}, {_maxValue}]";
        else
            return $"({_minValue}, {_maxValue})";
    }
}
```
This code defines a `RandomValueGenerator` class that manages a dynamic range for generating random values, both integers and floats, with customizable bounds. The class supports inclusive and exclusive ranges for both types. It implements methods to generate a random integer and a random float within the specified range, as well as a method to sample multiple random values of the same type consecutively without recalculating the range.

The `RandomValueGenerator` constructor takes two parameters: the minimum and maximum values for the range. If the minimum value is greater than the maximum value, an exception is thrown. The class also supports an optional third parameter that specifies whether the range should be inclusive or exclusive.

The `GenerateRandomInt` method generates a random integer within the specified range. If the range is empty (i.e., the minimum value equals the maximum value), the method returns the minimum value. The method also supports an optional parameter that specifies whether the range should be inclusive or exclusive.

The `GenerateRandomFloat` method generates a random float within the specified range. If the range is empty (i.e., the minimum value equals the maximum value), the method returns the minimum value. The method also supports an optional parameter that specifies whether the range should be inclusive or exclusive.

The `Reset` method resets the state of the generator to its initial values after a certain number of samples have been drawn. The method takes no parameters and does not return any value.

The `GenerateRandomInts` method generates multiple random integers within the specified range. If the range is empty (i.e., the minimum value equals the maximum value), the method returns an array with a single element equal to the minimum value. The method also supports an optional parameter that specifies whether the range should be inclusive or exclusive.

The `GenerateRandomFloats` method generates multiple random floats within the specified range. If the range is empty (i.e., the minimum value equals the maximum value), the method returns an array with a single element equal to the minimum value. The method also supports an optional parameter that specifies whether the range should be inclusive or exclusive.

The `ToString` method overrides the default behavior of the `Object.ToString` method and displays the current range of values being used by the generator. If the range is empty (i.e., the minimum value equals the maximum value), the method returns a string representation of the minimum value. The method also supports an optional parameter that specifies whether the range should be inclusive or exclusive.

The `RandomValueGenerator` class handles invalid range inputs gracefully by throwing appropriate exceptions if the minimum value is greater than the maximum value. The class also maintains state between calls to the sampling methods, ensuring consecutive calls produce different values until the range is reset.']

