asyncReduce(arr, (element) => {
  return element * 2;
}).then((result) => {
  console.log("Final partial sum:", result);
}).catch((err) => {
  console.error("Error occurred:", err);
});
```
This code will perform the reduction operation on the array of numbers using the callback function to multiply each element by 2. The function will handle any errors that may occur during the reduction operation and retry the operation with exponential backoff if necessary. Once the operation is complete, it will log the final partial sum or any error that occurred.']

