The `aes256cbc_encrypt` and `aes256cbc_decrypt` functions are used to encrypt and decrypt data using the AES-256-CBC cipher, respectively. These functions take the plaintext/ciphertext as input parameters and return the encrypted/decrypted data.

The `aes256cbc_cleanup` function is used to securely clean up and disable the AES-256-CBC cipher context when it is no longer needed. This function takes an `aes256cbc_ctx` pointer as input parameter and frees the memory allocated for the cipher context.

The code handles various edge cases, such as invalid password lengths or insufficient entropy in the environment, gracefully by returning appropriate error codes. The code also supports multiple concurrent cipher contexts without introducing race conditions or memory leaks.']

