The function logs the command execution status to a file named `background_processes.log` using the `fopen`, `snprintf`, and `fputs` functions. The log file is opened in append mode (`"a"`), so that new entries are added to the end of the file without overwriting existing content.

The function also includes a mechanism to limit the maximum number of concurrently running background processes to prevent resource exhaustion. This is achieved by using a global variable `num_processes` to keep track of the number of currently running processes, and by checking for the maximum allowed number of processes before starting a new process.

Finally, the function includes error handling to handle unexpected input and return appropriate error codes. The function returns -1 if any of the following conditions are met:

