* The `cmd` string is null or empty
* Forking a new process fails (i.e., `pid < 0`)
* Executing the command in the child process fails (i.e., `execvp` returns -1)
* Waiting for the child process to finish fails (i.e., `wait` returns -1)
* The command execution status is not an exit status (i.e., `WIFEXITED(status)` is false)
* The command execution status indicates a non-zero exit code (i.e., `WEXITSTATUS(status) != 0`)

In all other cases, the function returns the exit status of the executed command.']

