The function first uses json-c to parse the JSON string into a JSON object. If the parsing fails, it returns false immediately.

Next, the function checks for the required fields in the JSON object: access_token, expires_in, and token_type. It also checks for the optional field refresh_token if present. If any of these fields are missing or have an invalid value, the function returns false.

The function then checks for alphanumeric characters and hyphens in the access token and refresh token (if present). If any of these fields contain non-alphanumeric characters, the function returns false.

Finally, the function checks for integer overflow in the expires_in value by comparing it to INT_MAX. If the value is greater than INT_MAX, the function returns false.

The function uses json_object_put() to free any memory allocated during parsing and returns true if all checks pass successfully.']

