This function takes an input buffer and encrypts it using AES-256-CBC, Camellia-192-ECB, and ChaCha20-Poly1305. It then calculates SHA-256 and SHA-3 digests of the encrypted data and signs them using Ed25519. Finally, it combines the encrypted data, SHA-256 and SHA-3 digests, and Ed25519 signature into a single output buffer.

The function uses OpenSSL's EVP API to perform the cryptographic operations. It initializes an EVP context for each of the ciphers and digest algorithms it needs to use, and then adds them to the EVP context using the `EVP_add_cipher` and `EVP_add_digest` functions. It also sets up aliases for the digest algorithms using the `EVP_add_digest_alias` function.

The function encrypts the input data using AES-256-CBC and Camellia-192-ECB, and then calculates SHA-256 and SHA-3 digests of the encrypted data using the `EVP_DigestUpdate` and `EVP_DigestFinal` functions. It signs the SHA-256 and SHA-3 digests using Ed25519, and then combines the encrypted data, SHA-256 and SHA-3 digests, and Ed25519 signature into a single output buffer using `malloc` and `memcpy`.

The function returns the output buffer to the caller. It also cleans up the EVP contexts and buffers using the `EVP_CIPHER_CTX_free`, `EVP_MD_CTX_free`, and `EVP_PKEY_CTX_free` functions, as well as freeing any memory allocated by `malloc`.']

