The functions for managing memory and synchronization are implemented using mutexes to ensure that multiple threads can access the data structures simultaneously without causing data corruption. The linked list and hash table are resized automatically when they become full, while the node references are managed using a reference count to ensure that memory is only freed when all references are gone.

The system is designed to be modular and easily integrated with external logging and monitoring tools for tracking performance and errors. It also includes a mechanism for monitoring memory usage and triggering garbage collection manually when necessary to prevent out-of-memory conditions. The garbage collector prioritizes reclaiming memory from least recently used entries in the linked list and least frequently accessed entries in the hash table.

Overall, this implementation adheres to the constraints and provides a robust solution for handling complex scenarios in a multi-threaded environment.']

