To ensure that the allocated memory is properly managed to prevent leaks, the function includes a mechanism for tracking whether each record is in use or not. This allows the function to remove any unused records from the array periodically, which helps to minimize memory fragmentation over time.

The function also supports batch updates to the offset values for a specified range of keys, ensuring that these updates are atomic and do not disrupt ongoing operations. To achieve this, the function uses a mutex to prevent concurrent access to the array while updating the offset values.

Finally, the function includes real-time monitoring of memory usage and performance metrics, providing alerts if thresholds are exceeded. This allows developers to quickly identify any issues with the record manager and take appropriate action to resolve them."]

