3. Prioritization of critical logs over less important ones, ensuring that high-priority logs are logged first.
4. Distributed logging aggregation layer to offload some of the processing load from the main log management function, allowing for faster response times under heavy load.
5. Dynamic memory pool resizing and configuration support, allowing administrators to adjust the size of the log pool and the priority settings for asynchronous processing.
6. Robust error handling and recovery strategy to ensure data integrity and consistency, even in the event of system failures.
7. Support for multiple data persistence layers, including disk-based storage, in-memory databases, and cloud storage services.
8. APIs for easy integration with external tools and applications, enabling seamless log aggregation and analysis.']

